# ## Tool version pins (single source of truth)
#
# Every toolchain version this project needs lives in exactly one line of this
# file. Nothing else may hardcode a version.
#
# Consumers (read this file; never re-declare a pin):
#   - .devcontainer/Dockerfile   installs every tool below from these values
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml   installs the same set for CI, from these values
#   - make doctor                probes every key a present lane needs: a pin whose
#                                tool is missing or answers --version with a
#                                different number is an ERROR, and a key that no
#                                consumer installs is an ERROR too (see the CONSUMER
#                                RULE below). A key sitting under a `# -- <Lane> lane`
#                                heading is probed only when that lane is present in
#                                the checkout (tests/run.sh --lanes decides), so a
#                                shell-only project is never held hostage to the Go
#                                toolchain. Keys under a non-lane heading, like the
#                                repository-wide gates below, are always probed.
#
# CONSUMER RULE: each KEY below must be named by at least one consumer listed
# above. `make doctor` greps for every key in .devcontainer/Dockerfile and
# .github/workflows/ci.yml and fails the build on a key that appears in neither,
# because an unconsumed pin drifts silently and is indistinguishable from a tool
# that was quietly dropped from the pipeline. To retire a tool, delete the key
# AND its consumer line in the same commit.
#
# Format: KEY=value. No spaces around `=`, no quotes, no `export`, no command
# substitution, so the file stays POSIX-sourceable with `. ./tool-versions.env`
# and greppable by `make doctor`. Keep one key per line, in lane order.
#
# Version strings are stored WITHOUT a leading "v" even where the upstream GitHUB
# tag carries one; the consumer adds the prefix. An installer that 404s on a
# missing/extra "v" is a bug in the installer, not a reason to fork the format.
#
# Pins were read from the upstream registries on 2026-10-27: PyPI JSON API
# (pypi.org/pypi/<pkg>/json), the npm registry (registry.npmjs.org/<pkg>/latest),
# nodejs.org/dist/index.json, go.dev/VERSION, and the GitHub releases API for
# shellcheck, shfmt, bats-core, gitleaks and golangci-lint. Bump deliberately:
# a version bump is a code change that needs the test suite to run, not a
# drive-by edit.

# -- Shell lane (the default lane; see src/README.md) --------------------------
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (GitHub release binary), ci.yml
# (actions setup step), probed by `make doctor` as `shellcheck --version`.
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.11.0
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (Go install of mvdan/sh), ci.yml;
# `make fmt` and `make lint` both call it. Probed as `shfmt --version`.
SHFMT_VERSION=3.14.1
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (git clone + ./install.sh into
# /usr/local), ci.yml. `tests/run.sh` runs the shell lane with it.
BATS_VERSION=1.14.0
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (pipx), ci.yml; used by the YAML gate
# in `make lint`. Probed as `yamllint --version`.
YAMLLINT_VERSION=1.38.0

# -- Repository-wide gates (every lane) ----------------------------------------
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (pipx), ci.yml; `make hooks` calls it and
# .pre-commit-config.yaml pins matching hook revs. Probed as `pre-commit --version`.
PRE_COMMIT_VERSION=4.7.0
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (GitHub release binary), ci.yml secret
# scan step. Probed as `gitleaks version` (subcommand, not a flag).
GITLEAKS_VERSION=8.30.1
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (pipx), ci.yml; `make docs` uses it as the
# strict markdown/YAML formatter check. Probed as `prettier --version`.
PRETTIER_VERSION=3.9.10

# -- Python lane ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (pipx), ci.yml; `make lint` runs
# `ruff check` + `ruff format --check`. Probed as `ruff --version`.
RUFF_VERSION=0.17.3
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (pipx), ci.yml; `make lint` runs `mypy .`
# when the lane is present. Probed as `mypy --version`.
MYPY_VERSION=2.4.0
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (/opt/venv-test), ci.yml; this is the
# runner `tests/run.sh` invokes for the python lane. Probed as
# `python3 -m pytest --version`.
PYTEST_VERSION=9.1.1
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (same venv as pytest), python.yml. The
# `--cov` flag scripts/test-python.sh passes by default comes from this plugin, so
# an unpinned plugin would be an unpinned coverage gate. Probed as
# `python3 -c 'import pytest_cov; print(pytest_cov.__version__)'`.
PYTEST_COV_VERSION=7.1.0

# -- TypeScript lane -----------------------------------------------------------
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (nodejs.org tarball into /opt/node, and
# the source of npm for the lane), ci.yml setup-node. Probed as `node --version`.
NODE_VERSION=24.22.1
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (npm install -g), ci.yml; the lane's
# `tsc --noEmit` gate. Probed as `tsc --version`.
# Pinned below the npm `latest` tag (7.0.2): typescript-eslint declares
# `typescript >=4.8.4 <6.1.0` and typedoc's peer list ends at 6.0.x, so 7.x
# makes `npm ci` fail on peer resolution. 6.0.3 is the newest release both
# accept. Raise this only when both peers widen.
TYPESCRIPT_VERSION=6.0.3
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (npm install -g), ci.yml; `make lint` for
# the lane. Probed as `eslint --version`.
ESLINT_VERSION=10.13.0
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (npm install -g), ci.yml; this is the
# runner the typescript lane's `npm test` script calls. Probed as `vitest --version`.
VITEST_VERSION=5.0.5

# -- Go lane -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (go.dev/dl tarball into /usr/local/go),
# ci.yml setup-go; `tests/run.sh` runs `go test ./...` with it. Probed as `go version`.
GO_VERSION=1.27.3
# Installed by: .devcontainer/Dockerfile (GitHub release binary), ci.yml; the lane's
# lint gate. Probed as `golangci-lint --version`.
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=2.15.0
